=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch_dist_1_1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** OSPF routing daemon and network-statement configuration on `switch_dist_1_1` (the distribution-layer FRR router serving `host_1_1_1_1`'s pod).

**Mechanism:** `switch_dist_1_1` has no OSPF `network` statements in its FRR configuration and its `ospfd` process is not running. Without participation in OSPF, it cannot form an adjacency with `router_core_1` over their shared 172.16.0.6/31 link (area 0.0.0.1), cannot advertise the 10.1.1.0/24 access subnet into the OSPF domain, and — critically — cannot receive OSPF-learned routes for any remote prefix (10.200.0.0/24, 10.2.1.0/24, etc.). Its routing table therefore contains only its directly connected subnets.

**Localization:** When `host_1_1_1_1` (10.1.1.2) sends traffic to any off-subnet destination, its default gateway `switch_dist_1_1` (10.1.1.1) has no matching route and immediately returns an ICMP Destination Net Unreachable — exactly the "From 10.1.1.1: Destination Net Unreachable" observed in the direct-IP probe. The access switch `switch_access_1_1_1` is functioning correctly at L2 and is not involved.

**Root cause:** `switch_dist_1_1` is missing all OSPF `network` statements (and ospfd is not running), so it is completely isolated from the OSPF routing domain while every other FRR router in the topology participates normally.

**Fix:** Restore the OSPF configuration on `switch_dist_1_1` — add `network 10.1.1.0/24 area 0.0.0.1` and `network 172.16.0.6/31 area 0.0.0.1` (mirroring `switch_dist_2_1`'s working config, adjusted for pod-1 prefixes), then start `ospfd`. Do not replace `switch_access_1_1_1`; the fault lives entirely on `switch_dist_1_1`.
=== END ===